# PR / commit hygiene

When helping with commits or pull requests, align with `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.

## Before committing

- Tests for new/changed kit behavior or props (Jest and/or RSpec as applicable)
- Playground overrides updated for kits/props touched; regenerate with `yarn generate:docs-metadata`
- Stage regenerated metadata if the pre-commit hook updates it
- Do not commit secrets; do not skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests

## PR checklist (remind when creating/updating a PR)

- Use a Conventional Commit title as described in [Playbook PR titles](../../docs/PR_TITLES.md). If the PR has a Runway key, put it at the end.
- `milano` when ready for review
- Optional `inactive RC` when not an active RC

## Commit messages

Match recent history for individual commit messages. The Conventional Commit title check runs on the PR title.
